# vTPU handoff for Gemini

**Captured:** 2026-10-31 UTC  
**Repository:** https://github.com/wbic16/vtpu  
**Base branch:** `exo` — `f6845e1edbcde85031b881abb8f1b214870d8de8`  
**PR #1:** https://github.com/wbic16/vtpu/pull/1  
**Snapshot:** `codex/reality-gate-plan-20261031` — `4660934651a8afb065c4711b874b08b12becf213`  
**PR status at capture:** Open, unmerged  

## Contents

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `vtpu/` | The complete tracked vTPU source tree at PR #1's head, including the 315-line Reality Gate proposal (`docs/plans/reality-gate-2026-10-31.md`) |
| `vtpu-history.bundle` | Verified Git bundle with complete available history and refs (`exo`, `main`, PR #1 branch). This makes the source checkout reproducible without a live network connection. |
| `review/PR1-discussion.md` | Human-readable PR discussion capture, with original comment text, attribution, timestamp, and URL. |
| `review/PR1-discussion.json` | Machine-readable capture of the same discussion. |
| `review/Emise-RG001-review.txt` | Complete, byte-preserved commentary supplied directly by Will and attributed to Emise; not represented as a GitHub PR comment. |
| `review/REVIEW-SYNTHESIS.md` | Comparison of the Grok and Emise feedback with concrete follow-up questions for Gemini. |
| `review/GEMINI-REVIEW-BRIEF.md` | Work request for Gemini: compare plans, audit claims, and design a fair public challenge. |

The source directory includes **376 tracked files**. GitHub PR comments do not live in Git commits, so the discussion is separately snapshotted. The history bundle preserves branches and commits; it does **not** preserve GitHub discussion threads.

## Review status and caveat

Grok's review was visible on PR #1 and is included verbatim. At the GitHub discussion capture time, GitHub returned **one discussion comment**, posted by the `wbic16` account on behalf of Grok. No Emise-labeled comment, submitted review, or inline review thread was visible on PR #1. **Emise's full review was subsequently supplied by Will as a separate text attachment and is included verbatim in `review/Emise-RG001-review.txt`.** The two sources remain distinct: one verified GitHub discussion comment, one user-supplied reviewer artifact.

This snapshot deliberately preserves the **proposal as originally submitted**, before addressing Grok's or Emise's suggested changes. Gemini should evaluate both critiques without assuming either has already been incorporated.

## Reproducibility

From an extracted archive:

```bash
cd vtpu
cargo test
```

For full Git history, clone the sibling `vtpu-history.bundle` into a separate working directory and select the PR branch/commit. The bundle was verified with `git bundle verify` at creation. Do not mistake any historical README performance numbers for current measured hardware throughput without reproducing the associated experiment.

No build or test results are asserted by this handoff. Its purpose is to provide an exact source-and-discussion checkpoint for independent review.

