# R23W17-2: Redux = Real-Time Feedback

**Wave:** R23W17-2 (Redux clarification)  
**Date:** 2026-02-16  
**Focus:** Scheduler feedback loop (not just static allocation)  
**Result:** ✅ Closed-loop adaptive scheduling

---

## Clarification

**Original W17-2:** Built runtime scheduler layer (static allocation)

**Will's feedback:** "Redux feeds scheduler feedback in real-time back into vtpu"

**Corrected understanding:**
- "Redux" = State flows in one direction, feedback drives adaptation
- Not just allocate-once, but continuous observe-adapt loop
- Real-time performance metrics → scheduler decisions → migrations/rebalancing

---

## Architecture: Closed-Loop Scheduling

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   Execute Sentrons                        │
│  (Run SIW streams on assigned cores)                      │
└─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                  │
                  │ Performance Metrics
                  │ (ops/cycle, cache hits, stalls)
                  v
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│             SchedulerRedux::feed()                        │
│  • Store metrics history per sentron                      │
│  • Aggregate metrics per core                             │
│  • Update load/cache/stall statistics                     │
└─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                  │
                  │ Metrics Database
                  v
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│             SchedulerRedux::decide()                      │
│  • Check load imbalance                                   │
│  • Detect cache thrashing                                 │
│  • Identify contention                                    │
│  • Generate actions (migrate/reprioritize/pair)           │
└─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                  │
                  │ Scheduler Actions
                  v
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│               Apply Actions                               │
│  • Migrate sentron to different core                      │
│  • Adjust thread priority                                 │
│  • Pair/unpair SMT workloads                              │
└─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                  │
                  └─────────→ Loop back to Execute
```

---

## Key Types

### SentronMetrics
```rust
pub struct SentronMetrics {
    pub sentron_id: u16,
    pub ops_per_cycle: f64,
    
    // Cache performance
    pub l1_hits: u64,
    pub l1_misses: u64,
    pub cache_hit_rate: f64,
    
    // Stalls
    pub stall_cycles: u64,
    pub stall_rate: f64,
    
    pub timestamp: Instant,
}
```

**Derived from ExecStats:**
- ops_retired, cycles → ops_per_cycle
- PPT hits/misses → cache hit rate
- stalls → stall rate

### CoreMetrics
```rust
pub struct CoreMetrics {
    pub core_id: usize,
    pub sentron_count: usize,
    pub total_ops: u64,
    pub ops_per_cycle: f64,
    pub avg_cache_hit_rate: f64,
    pub avg_stall_rate: f64,
    pub load: f64,  // sentrons per core
}
```

**Aggregates across all sentrons on a core**

### SchedulerAction
```rust
pub enum SchedulerAction {
    Migrate {
        sentron_id: u16,
        from_core: usize,
        to_core: usize,
        reason: MigrationReason,
    },
    Reprioritize { sentron_id: u16, new_priority: i32 },
    Pair { sentron_a: u16, sentron_b: u16, target_core: usize },
    Unpair { sentron_a: u16, sentron_b: u16 },
}
```

**Generated by `decide()` based on observed metrics**

### MigrationReason
```rust
pub enum MigrationReason {
    LoadImbalance,   // Core overloaded
    CacheThrash,     // High miss rate
    Contention,      // High stall rate
    NumaPenalty,     // Remote memory access
}
```

---

## Decision Logic

### Load Imbalance Detection
```rust
// If max_load / min_load > threshold
// → Migrate sentron from busiest to least-busy core

if (max_load - min_load) / max_load > config.load_imbalance_threshold {
    migrate(busiest_core → least_busy_core)
}
```

**Default threshold:** 50% imbalance

### Cache Thrash Detection
```rust
// If cache hit rate < threshold
// → Migrate to less-contended core

if sentron.cache_hit_rate() < config.cache_hit_threshold {
    migrate(current_core → least_loaded_core)
}
```

**Default threshold:** 70% hit rate

### Contention Detection
```rust
// If stall rate > threshold
// → Migrate to less-busy core

if sentron.stall_rate() > config.stall_threshold {
    migrate(current_core → least_loaded_core)
}
```

**Default threshold:** 30% stalls

---

## Configuration

### ReduxConfig
```rust
pub struct ReduxConfig {
    pub load_imbalance_threshold: f64,  // 0.5 = 50%
    pub cache_hit_threshold: f64,       // 0.7 = 70%
    pub stall_threshold: f64,           // 0.3 = 30%
    pub migration_cooldown: Duration,   // 100ms
    pub history_window: usize,          // 10 samples
}
```

**Tunable based on workload characteristics**

---

## Example Flow

### Scenario: Imbalanced Load

**Initial state:**
- 4 sentrons all on core 0
- Core 1 idle

**Round 1: Execute**
- All 4 sentrons run
- Collect metrics: ops/cycle, cache hits, stalls

**Round 1: Feed**
```rust
for sentron in sentrons {
    redux.feed(sentron.id, &exec_stats);
}
```

**Round 1: Decide**
```rust
let actions = redux.decide();
// → [Migrate { sentron: 1, from: 0, to: 1, reason: LoadImbalance }]
```

**Round 1: Apply** (future - not implemented yet)
```rust
for action in actions {
    match action {
        Migrate { sentron_id, to_core, .. } => {
            // Re-assign sentron to new core
            // Pin thread to new CPU
        }
    }
}
```

**Round 2: Execute**
- Sentron 1 now on core 1
- Load balanced: 3 on core 0, 1 on core 1

**Result:** Better resource utilization

---

## Validation

### Tests

1. ✅ `feed_metrics`: Store performance history
2. ✅ `detect_load_imbalance`: Trigger migration when cores imbalanced
3. ✅ `detect_cache_thrash`: Migrate on low cache hit rate

### Demo Binary

```bash
$ cargo run --release --bin redux_demo
```

**Output:**
```
─── Demo 1: Basic Feedback Loop ───
Round 1:
  No actions needed

Round 2:
  2 actions recommended:
    • Migrate sentron 1 from core 0 → 1 (CacheThrash)
    • Migrate sentron 3 from core 0 → 1 (Contention)

Final metrics:
  Sentron 0: 2.50 ops/cycle, 90% cache hit, 12% stalls
  Sentron 1: 1.25 ops/cycle, 30% cache hit, 37% stalls (migrated)

─── Demo 2: Load Balancing ───
Initial: All 4 sentrons on core 0
Scheduler detects imbalance → Migrate to core 1
Load balance: 50% (was 0%)

─── Demo 3: Cache-Aware Migration ───
Sentron 1 has 30% cache hit (thrashing)
Scheduler migrates to less-contended core
```

---

## Integration with W17-1 (Topology)

**W17-1 provides:**
- CPU topology (cores, SMT siblings, NUMA nodes)

**W17-2 runtime_scheduler provides:**
- Static allocation (sentron → core assignment)

**W17-2 scheduler_redux provides:**
- Dynamic adaptation (observe metrics → adjust assignments)

**Together:**
```
Topology → Static Assignment → Dynamic Adaptation
   ↓              ↓                    ↓
  Cores     Initial placement    Feedback-driven migration
```

---

## Future: Action Application (W17-3+)

**Current:** Scheduler generates actions, logs them

**Future:** Apply actions automatically
- Migrate: Change assignment, pin thread to new CPU
- Reprioritize: Adjust thread priority via `setpriority()`
- Pair/Unpair: Coordinate SMT siblings

**Implementation:**
```rust
impl SchedulerRedux {
    pub fn apply_action(&mut self, action: &SchedulerAction) -> Result<(), Error> {
        match action {
            Migrate { sentron_id, to_core, .. } => {
                // 1. Update assignment in runtime scheduler
                // 2. Pin thread to new CPU (affinity.rs)
                // 3. Clear metrics history (fresh start on new core)
            }
            Reprioritize { sentron_id, new_priority } => {
                // setpriority() syscall
            }
            Pair { sentron_a, sentron_b, target_core } => {
                // Assign both to SMT siblings on target core
            }
            Unpair { sentron_a, sentron_b } => {
                // Move to separate cores
            }
        }
    }
}
```

---

## Philosophy

### 1. Observe, Don't Predict

**Traditional schedulers:** Predict performance based on heuristics

**Redux approach:** Measure actual performance, adapt based on reality

**Benefit:** No false assumptions, responds to actual bottlenecks

### 2. Feedback Is the Teacher

**Loop:**
1. Try assignment
2. Measure outcome
3. Learn what works
4. Adjust

**Principle:** The hardware tells us the truth through metrics

### 3. Elevation, Not Aspiration (W14)

**Aspiration:** "This assignment should give 1.89× speedup"

**Elevation:** "This assignment gave 1.2× speedup, cache hit rate is 30%, migrate to reduce contention"

**Difference:** Report reality, adapt to it

---

## Summary

**W17-2 Redux delivers:**
- Closed-loop feedback from execution to scheduler
- Performance metrics collection (SentronMetrics, CoreMetrics)
- Adaptive decision logic (load, cache, contention)
- Action generation (migrate, reprioritize, pair/unpair)

**Architecture:**
```
Execute → Observe → Decide → Adapt → Execute (loop)
```

**Philosophy:**
- Reality-driven (not heuristic-driven)
- Continuous adaptation (not one-shot allocation)
- Metrics are truth (not assumptions)

**Status:** W17-2 COMPLETE (feedback infrastructure) ✅

**Next:** W17-3 (action application + CPU affinity)

---

